        "original_id": "cf4dc0cd-1dde-5f69-9ec6-416ab17b91f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mabel Keyes Babcock, Henry H. Babcock, Mary Porter (Keyes) Babcock, William Bradford\n- Places: Somerville, Massachusetts, Plymouth Colony\n- Roles: botanist, Governor of Plymouth Colony\n- Documents: Mayflower Compact, Of Plymouth Plantation\n\nFacts:\n- William Bradford was a signatory to the Mayflower Compact.\n- Between 1621 and 1657, William Bradford served intermittently as Governor of Plymouth Colony for about 30 years.\n- William Bradford's journal \"Of Plymouth Plantation\" covered the years 1620 to 1657 in Plymouth.\n- Mabel Keyes Babcock was born in Somerville, Massachusetts, on May 20, 1862.\n- Mabel Keyes Babcock was the daughter of botanist Henry H. Babcock and Mary Porter (Keyes) Babcock.\n- Mabel Keyes Babcock was a descendant of William Bradford.",
